1
00:00:57,058 --> 00:00:58,637
You all killed my husband.

2
00:01:16,632 --> 00:01:18,220
Dong, I thought you were dead.

3
00:01:18,718 --> 00:01:19,718
Dong.

4
00:01:20,623 --> 00:01:21,708
Have you also heard,

5
00:01:21,740 --> 00:01:23,452
that she killed those
who kidnapped her?

6
00:01:23,477 --> 00:01:24,481
What?

7
00:01:24,506 --> 00:01:27,842
Keep your mouth shut if you
don't want to end up like your friend.

8
00:01:28,809 --> 00:01:30,049
You're an assassin, aren't you?

9
00:01:31,241 --> 00:01:33,494
What if I was the one
who killed your friends?

10
00:01:43,974 --> 00:01:44,975
Like I've said,

11
00:01:45,805 --> 00:01:47,947
Yaji is not our enemy here.

12
00:01:47,972 --> 00:01:51,059
The purpose of this launch
is to expose the enemy.

13
00:01:51,084 --> 00:01:52,585
We're not the only sniper here.

14
00:01:52,658 --> 00:01:53,658
There are others.

15
00:02:04,016 --> 00:02:05,776
Mr. Roswell. Ma'am Aemie.

16
00:02:06,963 --> 00:02:07,963
Boss.

17
00:02:12,114 --> 00:02:14,686
Damn! You guys are
looking so handsome.

18
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:18,389
Good thing they
finally started arriving.

19
00:02:18,646 --> 00:02:20,547
I don't know anyone
here except them.

20
00:02:24,883 --> 00:02:25,914
Oh.

21
00:02:25,939 --> 00:02:26,939
Hey.

22
00:02:27,539 --> 00:02:28,539
Kaizer.

23
00:02:28,630 --> 00:02:29,630
Are you okay?

24
00:02:29,669 --> 00:02:31,546
Why are you slapping yourself?

25
00:02:32,737 --> 00:02:34,280
No, I'm fine, Ma'am Aemie.

26
00:02:34,971 --> 00:02:36,171
Just trying to wake myself up.

27
00:02:46,441 --> 00:02:48,521
Good thing they got us
all seated at the same table.

28
00:02:49,045 --> 00:02:50,088
Keep me company, okay?

29
00:02:50,119 --> 00:02:51,119
Psst. Hey.

30
00:03:06,242 --> 00:03:07,493
So boring.

31
00:03:08,561 --> 00:03:10,480
I guess I'll just take a selfie.

32
00:03:15,656 --> 00:03:16,740
Like I've said,

33
00:03:17,446 --> 00:03:19,823
Yaji isn't our enemy here.

34
00:03:20,635 --> 00:03:24,013
The purpose of this launch
is to expose the enemy.

35
00:03:29,905 --> 00:03:31,156
Fifteen minutes to go.

36
00:03:32,402 --> 00:03:33,402
Huh?

37
00:03:33,548 --> 00:03:34,549
What's that, Dong?

38
00:03:39,523 --> 00:03:40,941
Sebastian's bored.

39
00:03:40,988 --> 00:03:42,073
Bye!

40
00:03:53,124 --> 00:03:54,292
Twelve minutes.

41
00:03:58,707 --> 00:04:00,292
I'll just wait for you guys.

42
00:04:02,463 --> 00:04:04,340
Why are you counting down, Dong?

43
00:04:05,574 --> 00:04:06,908
Just eat, wife.

44
00:04:19,427 --> 00:04:20,511
Ten minutes.

45
00:04:29,321 --> 00:04:30,948
What's going on?

46
00:04:31,944 --> 00:04:34,767
Why is everyone leaving?

47
00:05:34,031 --> 00:05:36,283
I bet you came here
to see your daughter.

48
00:05:37,938 --> 00:05:39,856
Why haven't you joined them?

49
00:05:40,088 --> 00:05:41,088
No.

50
00:05:41,657 --> 00:05:44,044
Actually, I came
here to see you dead.

51
00:05:47,461 --> 00:05:48,462
Just kidding.

52
00:05:49,344 --> 00:05:51,038
Don't take it too seriously.

53
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:52,580
It might come true.

54
00:05:53,302 --> 00:05:56,221
Well, see you around, Mrs. Ferrer.

55
00:05:56,791 --> 00:05:59,377
Anyways, if you want
to know my name,

56
00:05:59,788 --> 00:06:00,998
Cyd Garnett.

57
00:06:01,966 --> 00:06:02,966
Noted.

58
00:06:08,745 --> 00:06:10,038
Mr. Roswell.

59
00:06:11,122 --> 00:06:12,123
Mr. Ferrer.

60
00:06:13,043 --> 00:06:14,086
Good to see you here.

61
00:06:14,523 --> 00:06:15,523
Thank you.

62
00:06:16,325 --> 00:06:18,494
This is Violet Swansea.

63
00:06:19,110 --> 00:06:20,486
Hello, good evening.

64
00:06:24,783 --> 00:06:26,910
Is she the wife of
Caileigh's father?

65
00:06:29,044 --> 00:06:31,541
I thought Caileigh's
mother was dead.

66
00:06:33,682 --> 00:06:35,225
Good evening, young lady.

67
00:06:36,031 --> 00:06:37,031
Oh.

68
00:06:37,665 --> 00:06:40,585
I wasn't able to formally
introduce my wife to you, sir,

69
00:06:40,610 --> 00:06:41,944
the last time we met.

70
00:06:42,518 --> 00:06:44,561
This is my wife,

71
00:06:45,561 --> 00:06:47,646
Aemie Ferrer-Roswell.

72
00:06:48,067 --> 00:06:51,403
The daughter of
Alyana Heartily-Ferrer.

73
00:06:54,383 --> 00:06:55,383
Zeke?

74
00:07:13,851 --> 00:07:15,686
What does this mean, kid?

75
00:07:16,813 --> 00:07:18,189
Welcome to our party.

76
00:08:04,026 --> 00:08:06,154
Violet, I thought you
were on our side?

77
00:08:07,530 --> 00:08:09,824
Sorry to disappoint you, Alyana.

78
00:08:10,283 --> 00:08:14,328
I'm the one who killed your
family, the Roswell family too.

79
00:08:14,996 --> 00:08:17,707
And I'm planning to
continue this set-up

80
00:08:18,082 --> 00:08:21,544
through the next
generations of your families.

81
00:08:22,128 --> 00:08:23,504
You've gone crazy!

82
00:08:23,504 --> 00:08:24,504
Yes!

83
00:08:25,006 --> 00:08:27,258
I'm crazy!

84
00:08:28,467 --> 00:08:31,620
Crazily in love
with your husband.

85
00:08:34,891 --> 00:08:36,142
So long!

86
00:08:36,559 --> 00:08:38,394
Alyana Heartily-Ferrer!

87
00:08:41,230 --> 00:08:42,815
Ladies and gentlemen,

88
00:08:43,024 --> 00:08:46,402
please join me in welcoming
Mrs. Aemie Roswell,

89
00:08:46,694 --> 00:08:50,907
as we celebrate this exciting
launch in the toy industry.

90
00:08:52,658 --> 00:08:56,120
Eiji and Roswell need
to know about this.

91
00:09:06,005 --> 00:09:07,005
Mei.

92
00:09:07,965 --> 00:09:09,325
How about you just
ditch your plan?

93
00:09:10,348 --> 00:09:11,362
What?

94
00:09:11,427 --> 00:09:13,137
Are you out of your mind, Cass?

95
00:09:13,554 --> 00:09:15,389
She's absolutely fine, sis.

96
00:09:26,442 --> 00:09:28,694
I'll take care of my
sister, Miss Heather.

97
00:09:29,570 --> 00:09:30,738
What are you doing here, Max?

98
00:09:30,738 --> 00:09:31,906
Where are you going, Cass?

99
00:09:32,281 --> 00:09:35,034
I will obey the
order of the Queen.

100
00:09:36,744 --> 00:09:40,998
As we celebrate this exciting
launch in the toy industry.

101
00:09:42,250 --> 00:09:44,919
Let's give her a round of applause.

102
00:09:45,670 --> 00:09:46,712
Good luck, wife.

103
00:09:51,384 --> 00:09:52,384
Sis, don't!

104
00:09:56,222 --> 00:09:57,222
Oh, shucks.

105
00:09:59,879 --> 00:10:01,492
There's a blackout!

106
00:10:01,811 --> 00:10:03,479
- Guys, what's happening?
- Zeke?

107
00:10:03,479 --> 00:10:04,855
This isn't part of the plan.

108
00:10:05,299 --> 00:10:08,258
- Where are you?
- Just hold on to me tightly, Ma'am Aemie.

109
00:10:08,294 --> 00:10:09,294
Come on.

110
00:10:10,069 --> 00:10:11,069
Where are we going?

111
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:12,320
Just hold on.

112
00:10:12,530 --> 00:10:14,448
- Okay.
- We'll explain everything later.

113
00:10:30,923 --> 00:10:31,923
Queen.

114
00:10:32,591 --> 00:10:34,093
I know where Aemie
and the others are.

115
00:10:34,552 --> 00:10:35,845
I'll take you to them.

116
00:10:36,262 --> 00:10:37,262
Who are you?

117
00:10:37,805 --> 00:10:39,348
I'm Fauzia Arcadia, ma'am.

118
00:10:40,224 --> 00:10:41,267
Arcadia?

119
00:10:43,252 --> 00:10:47,131
By chance, you know
Simon Arcadia and his wife?

120
00:10:47,438 --> 00:10:48,731
Pauline Crest.

121
00:10:49,206 --> 00:10:50,251
Yes, ma'am.

122
00:10:50,276 --> 00:10:51,694
They're my parents.

123
00:10:52,608 --> 00:10:53,608
Let's go.

124
00:10:54,679 --> 00:10:56,765
Fauzia, where are you going?

125
00:10:57,908 --> 00:10:59,243
You traitorous bitch!

126
00:10:59,702 --> 00:11:01,078
I'm not a traitor.

127
00:11:01,412 --> 00:11:03,080
I've never been your ally.

128
00:11:11,756 --> 00:11:14,759
Fuck, I don't
have time for this.

129
00:11:15,843 --> 00:11:16,843
Let's go.

130
00:11:17,053 --> 00:11:18,053
Come on.

131
00:11:29,106 --> 00:11:30,900
Where do you think you're going?

132
00:11:34,820 --> 00:11:36,697
You cannot run away from me.

133
00:11:37,281 --> 00:11:38,324
Violet!

134
00:11:38,741 --> 00:11:39,950
You bitch!

135
00:12:06,060 --> 00:12:08,479
Let's go back! Don't you
want to go back?

136
00:12:13,692 --> 00:12:15,111
Is this part of the program?

137
00:12:16,737 --> 00:12:18,239
Go, Jacob!
Do your best, hurry!

138
00:12:21,409 --> 00:12:22,409
Come on, Ma'am Aemie.

139
00:12:24,370 --> 00:12:25,955
- You were awesome back there, man!
- Let's go.

140
00:12:25,955 --> 00:12:27,039
You killed him?

141
00:12:28,521 --> 00:12:29,606
Guardian angel!

142
00:12:29,681 --> 00:12:30,890
Shit. Fauzia.

143
00:12:31,252 --> 00:12:32,253
Mommy!

144
00:12:32,420 --> 00:12:34,380
- I'll just get the car.
- Mommy!

145
00:12:36,215 --> 00:12:38,926
- Mommy, what happened?
- Vash! Hurry!

146
00:12:39,581 --> 00:12:40,594
What happened?

147
00:12:40,594 --> 00:12:43,224
- Mommy, who did this to you?
- Vash, hurry!

148
00:12:43,249 --> 00:12:44,281
Baby Ae.

149
00:12:44,306 --> 00:12:45,599
- Mommy.
- Your dad...

150
00:12:46,058 --> 00:12:47,058
Alive.

151
00:12:47,446 --> 00:12:48,476
Dad?

152
00:12:48,561 --> 00:12:49,883
- Alive.
- Alive?

153
00:12:51,272 --> 00:12:53,858
I don't understand you.
Mommy, what?

154
00:12:54,608 --> 00:12:55,651
Please, Baby Ae.

155
00:12:56,235 --> 00:12:57,361
[mumbling]

156
00:12:57,361 --> 00:12:59,822
Mommy, who did this to you?

157
00:13:00,131 --> 00:13:01,924
Who did this to you, Mommy?

158
00:13:01,949 --> 00:13:03,826
Who? Mommy!

159
00:13:07,210 --> 00:13:08,239
Roswell.

160
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:12,500
Zeke?

161
00:13:18,841 --> 00:13:19,841
Wife.

162
00:13:36,859 --> 00:13:39,528
So, any update
on their condition?

163
00:13:39,945 --> 00:13:41,363
Are they finally dead yet?

164
00:13:44,073 --> 00:13:45,073
What?

165
00:13:46,118 --> 00:13:47,453
Goddamn it!

166
00:13:50,998 --> 00:13:51,998
What happened?

167
00:13:52,703 --> 00:13:54,371
They were rushed
to the hospital.

168
00:13:55,033 --> 00:13:56,701
They're in the
operating room now.

169
00:13:58,122 --> 00:13:59,540
I'll handle Arcadia.

170
00:14:00,799 --> 00:14:02,510
Who wants to join Valkyrie?

171
00:14:03,106 --> 00:14:04,153
Can I?

172
00:14:04,178 --> 00:14:05,346
No, not you.

173
00:14:05,721 --> 00:14:07,139
It's too dangerous.

174
00:14:07,848 --> 00:14:09,308
I'll go with her.

175
00:14:11,014 --> 00:14:12,808
We're not even Swansea.

176
00:14:13,521 --> 00:14:14,980
Why are you volunteering?

177
00:14:16,208 --> 00:14:18,377
We want to take down
Roswell, don't we?

178
00:14:19,511 --> 00:14:21,805
Whoever wants him gone,
I'm helping them.

179
00:14:27,159 --> 00:14:29,411
Roswells, Yaji.

180
00:14:30,079 --> 00:14:34,041
Two groups full of dumb members.

181
00:14:34,792 --> 00:14:36,835
Let them fight
each other to death.

182
00:14:47,012 --> 00:14:50,307
And administer this to
Arcadia in the hospital.

183
00:14:55,271 --> 00:14:56,730
It's for hypertension.

184
00:14:57,147 --> 00:14:58,440
But it's also known

185
00:14:58,440 --> 00:15:01,342
to weaken memories
of traumatic experiences

186
00:15:01,610 --> 00:15:05,489
once given shortly
before the event.

187
00:15:06,282 --> 00:15:07,616
Why don't we just kill her?

188
00:15:07,948 --> 00:15:11,118
Because that's how I want it!

189
00:15:16,303 --> 00:15:17,303
Let's go?

190
00:15:24,049 --> 00:15:25,718
I'll go with you, Valkyrie.

191
00:15:26,468 --> 00:15:28,429
I wanna know what
happened to Ezekiel.

192
00:15:29,346 --> 00:15:30,346
Suit yourself.

193
00:15:42,443 --> 00:15:43,444
Zeke.

194
00:15:50,148 --> 00:15:51,148
Did you—

195
00:15:56,165 --> 00:15:58,376
Did you really do that to Mommy?

196
00:16:03,297 --> 00:16:04,298
No.

197
00:16:36,997 --> 00:16:39,083
Is there a problem,
Ezekiel Roswell?

198
00:16:44,380 --> 00:16:45,380
What?

199
00:16:46,965 --> 00:16:47,965
None.

200
00:17:10,364 --> 00:17:13,575
I'm here to see my
daughter and wife.

201
00:17:15,452 --> 00:17:16,452
Huh?

202
00:17:17,079 --> 00:17:18,163
What is Uncle talking about?

203
00:17:18,163 --> 00:17:20,457
Caileigh isn't here, right, Momo?

204
00:17:20,666 --> 00:17:23,210
How would I know?
Just shut up, Wakwak!

205
00:17:27,089 --> 00:17:28,089
Aemie.

206
00:17:31,051 --> 00:17:32,344
Your father is here.

207
00:17:40,185 --> 00:17:41,185
Fa—

208
00:17:41,228 --> 00:17:42,396
Father?

209
00:17:42,521 --> 00:17:43,521
What?

210
00:17:46,150 --> 00:17:47,568
What do you mean?

211
00:17:48,902 --> 00:17:49,987
Mr. Ferrer...

212
00:17:51,363 --> 00:17:53,240
is your biological father.

213
00:17:58,287 --> 00:18:00,372
I don't— I don't understand you.

214
00:18:00,497 --> 00:18:03,000
- Mommy!
- Your dad. Alive.

215
00:18:03,792 --> 00:18:04,792
Dad?

216
00:18:05,210 --> 00:18:06,210
Alive?

217
00:18:10,924 --> 00:18:11,967
I remember.

218
00:18:13,218 --> 00:18:14,386
That's why,

219
00:18:15,721 --> 00:18:17,055
Mommy said,

220
00:18:18,057 --> 00:18:20,851
she was saying
"dad" and "alive."

221
00:18:22,730 --> 00:18:25,065
Because she's
trying to tell me that...

222
00:18:27,597 --> 00:18:28,848
you're still alive.

223
00:18:33,833 --> 00:18:35,001
Excuse me.

224
00:18:53,550 --> 00:18:55,010
I can't believe this.

225
00:18:56,303 --> 00:18:57,471
You're here.

226
00:18:58,013 --> 00:18:59,013
Alive.

227
00:19:03,075 --> 00:19:04,868
You're Amesyl, right?

228
00:19:09,242 --> 00:19:10,341
I'm your uncle.

229
00:19:11,746 --> 00:19:15,119
Your father, Alexander,
was my cousin.

230
00:19:17,736 --> 00:19:22,365
I'm sorry, but I won't believe it
until Auntie says it herself.

231
00:19:22,734 --> 00:19:23,734
Cuz.

232
00:19:25,437 --> 00:19:26,437
Believe him.

233
00:19:27,815 --> 00:19:30,193
Mommy told me before
she lost consciousness.

234
00:19:41,098 --> 00:19:42,099
Doc?

235
00:19:42,358 --> 00:19:43,610
- Doc.
- Doc.

236
00:19:44,054 --> 00:19:45,076
What's the news?

237
00:19:45,227 --> 00:19:46,603
Ms. Arcadia is fine.

238
00:19:46,937 --> 00:19:50,649
She has a lot of broken bones, but
she'll recover from them in no time.

239
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:52,735
What about Auntie Yana?

240
00:19:53,861 --> 00:19:55,495
As for Ms. Heartily,

241
00:19:55,665 --> 00:19:57,584
the operation is still ongoing.

242
00:19:58,616 --> 00:20:01,244
The gunshot wound
caused a lot of blood loss.

243
00:20:01,468 --> 00:20:03,470
She's in a critical
state as of now,

244
00:20:03,537 --> 00:20:05,330
but we're doing
everything we can.

245
00:20:05,664 --> 00:20:06,664
Excuse me.

246
00:20:45,211 --> 00:20:46,211
Thanks.

247
00:21:12,347 --> 00:21:14,808
Dear, take a seat.

248
00:21:20,697 --> 00:21:21,697
Cuz.

249
00:21:21,831 --> 00:21:23,917
Where have you been?
I've been looking for you.

250
00:21:30,499 --> 00:21:32,417
Hey, aren't you going
to pay attention to me?

251
00:21:36,317 --> 00:21:37,327
Aemie,

252
00:21:37,352 --> 00:21:41,105
you should stay at my mansion for
now while your mom is recovering.

253
00:21:42,038 --> 00:21:43,038
Is that okay?

254
00:21:43,303 --> 00:21:44,346
Wait.

255
00:21:45,152 --> 00:21:47,905
What about Zeke if cuz
stays at your mansion?

256
00:21:48,934 --> 00:21:50,858
Not that I mean to meddle,

257
00:21:51,062 --> 00:21:54,690
but shouldn't you ask her
husband for permission first?

258
00:21:58,110 --> 00:22:00,404
Cuz, it's okay.

259
00:22:02,239 --> 00:22:03,254
It's okay?

260
00:22:03,279 --> 00:22:04,300
Oh.

261
00:22:04,325 --> 00:22:05,325
Apparently, it's okay.

262
00:22:05,951 --> 00:22:07,035
Then it's settled.

263
00:22:07,369 --> 00:22:09,287
Aemie and you,

264
00:22:09,580 --> 00:22:11,374
will live in the Ferrer Mansion.

265
00:22:12,310 --> 00:22:14,412
Me? Even I am coming along?

266
00:22:16,221 --> 00:22:17,221
Huh?

267
00:22:45,073 --> 00:22:46,491
Welcome home.

268
00:22:48,182 --> 00:22:49,850
It's beautiful, right?

269
00:22:51,727 --> 00:22:53,104
Do you like your room?

270
00:23:00,672 --> 00:23:01,672
It's okay.

271
00:23:04,009 --> 00:23:05,552
I will let you settle down.

272
00:23:13,294 --> 00:23:15,796
Cuz, aren't you planning
to finish your food?

273
00:23:24,237 --> 00:23:26,323
What time do you want
to go to the hospital?

274
00:23:38,210 --> 00:23:40,879
Aemie dear, do you want to shop?

275
00:23:41,379 --> 00:23:42,714
Buy some clothes.

276
00:23:43,215 --> 00:23:44,633
Let's have a relaxation day.

277
00:23:44,800 --> 00:23:45,800
No.

278
00:23:46,468 --> 00:23:47,677
I'm going to the hospital.

279
00:23:48,929 --> 00:23:50,514
Come on, dear.

280
00:23:51,051 --> 00:23:53,928
Don't stress yourself
out too much.

281
00:23:54,424 --> 00:23:58,052
Besides, we need to bond
like mother and daughter.

282
00:24:00,190 --> 00:24:01,190
No!

283
00:24:02,734 --> 00:24:04,027
My mommy is still alive.

284
00:24:04,778 --> 00:24:06,113
I don't need a substitute.

285
00:24:15,038 --> 00:24:16,623
Oh, Cuz!

286
00:24:16,873 --> 00:24:18,834
You haven't finished your food!

287
00:24:23,547 --> 00:24:24,840
I pity her.

288
00:24:26,341 --> 00:24:27,634
She's so down.

289
00:24:33,014 --> 00:24:34,099
How about you, Amesyl?

290
00:24:34,724 --> 00:24:36,309
Do you want to join
me for shopping?

291
00:24:37,561 --> 00:24:40,355
I'll accompany
Cuz to the hospital.

292
00:24:51,533 --> 00:24:52,534
Here.

293
00:24:54,850 --> 00:24:56,060
Take it slow.

294
00:25:00,810 --> 00:25:02,520
You really don't
remember anything?

295
00:25:03,568 --> 00:25:04,568
Fauzia?

296
00:25:11,130 --> 00:25:12,840
What happened anyway?

297
00:25:15,614 --> 00:25:18,700
It might be better if I don't tell
you yet, that's what Doc said.

298
00:25:20,203 --> 00:25:21,859
Apparently, the trauma makes you

299
00:25:21,884 --> 00:25:24,902
unable to remember some of what
happened over the past few days.

300
00:25:28,987 --> 00:25:30,071
Any news?

301
00:25:31,323 --> 00:25:32,407
She's okay.

302
00:25:33,241 --> 00:25:34,284
What about Boss?

303
00:25:34,284 --> 00:25:35,327
How is he?

304
00:25:37,245 --> 00:25:38,245
I don't know.

305
00:25:39,456 --> 00:25:41,499
Lerwick and I still
haven't seen Boss.

306
00:25:45,515 --> 00:25:48,101
So, it's still unclear what
our next plan of action is.

307
00:25:56,223 --> 00:25:57,307
Excuse me, sir.

308
00:25:57,307 --> 00:25:59,731
The patient needs to
take her medication now.

309
00:25:59,756 --> 00:26:00,756
Okay.

310
00:26:12,964 --> 00:26:14,048
Here's the water.

311
00:26:15,563 --> 00:26:16,647
Slowly.

312
00:26:22,938 --> 00:26:24,023
Are you okay?

313
00:26:24,575 --> 00:26:25,575
Thank you.

314
00:26:36,263 --> 00:26:37,847
Boss, we'll just be outside.

315
00:26:59,286 --> 00:27:02,372
Do you know how much
I love your mom?

316
00:27:05,641 --> 00:27:07,559
For twenty years.

317
00:27:08,548 --> 00:27:10,717
I felt like I was going crazy.

318
00:27:11,842 --> 00:27:13,177
Breathing...

319
00:27:14,884 --> 00:27:17,304
but life felt meaningless.

320
00:27:20,677 --> 00:27:24,013
Twenty hardest years.

321
00:27:26,938 --> 00:27:30,900
Twenty long years
that I thought...

322
00:27:32,152 --> 00:27:34,654
your mom was really gone.

323
00:27:38,244 --> 00:27:39,912
I was happy when...

324
00:27:40,943 --> 00:27:42,492
I found you.

325
00:27:44,926 --> 00:27:47,386
And it's all thanks to Violet.

326
00:27:48,373 --> 00:27:49,373
That night,

327
00:27:50,193 --> 00:27:52,461
when Roswell introduced you to me.

328
00:27:54,398 --> 00:27:56,566
Violet had already told me that

329
00:27:57,719 --> 00:28:00,096
she had been looking for
your mom for a long time.

330
00:28:01,848 --> 00:28:05,518
That night, I thought she had died.

331
00:28:06,799 --> 00:28:09,760
We had no choice but to run.

332
00:28:12,233 --> 00:28:14,611
Your mom and I got separated...

333
00:28:16,738 --> 00:28:20,367
we sent her ahead
with your Auntie Sylvia.

334
00:28:22,118 --> 00:28:23,328
We agreed...

335
00:28:24,996 --> 00:28:28,375
to meet at the end of a bridge.

336
00:28:30,377 --> 00:28:31,377
But, but...

337
00:28:32,587 --> 00:28:34,214
but after the battle...

338
00:28:37,050 --> 00:28:38,843
I couldn't find her.

339
00:28:40,178 --> 00:28:42,055
I waited for so long.

340
00:28:44,599 --> 00:28:48,228
But all that came was Violet.

341
00:28:49,479 --> 00:28:53,942
Then she told me that
the Roswells had killed

342
00:28:54,692 --> 00:28:56,027
your mom,

343
00:28:57,028 --> 00:28:58,363
Sylvia,

344
00:28:59,197 --> 00:29:00,824
Amesyl.

345
00:29:07,205 --> 00:29:08,456
Roswells?

346
00:29:10,083 --> 00:29:11,209
I'm sorry, dear.

347
00:29:12,335 --> 00:29:13,920
But that's the truth.

348
00:29:15,296 --> 00:29:17,674
The Roswells are our enemies.

349
00:29:21,261 --> 00:29:24,722
But now that I have
you and your mom again,

350
00:29:25,223 --> 00:29:28,935
I won't let you slip away again.

351
00:29:59,883 --> 00:30:02,469
I don't understand, why
did you come here anyway?

352
00:30:03,094 --> 00:30:04,637
I already told you, Jerson.

353
00:30:04,637 --> 00:30:06,764
I'm just here to
check on Ezekiel.

354
00:30:07,098 --> 00:30:08,266
Be careful.

355
00:30:08,558 --> 00:30:10,393
There are a lot of Yaji
and Roswells here now.

356
00:30:14,181 --> 00:30:15,807
Uhh. Excuse me.

357
00:30:18,193 --> 00:30:20,278
You're Arcadia's nurse, right?

358
00:30:20,278 --> 00:30:21,278
Yes, I am.

359
00:30:24,824 --> 00:30:25,950
You know what to do.

360
00:30:26,826 --> 00:30:28,077
I'll take care of it.

361
00:30:34,058 --> 00:30:35,084
Alright, Jerson.

362
00:30:35,109 --> 00:30:36,109
I'll go ahead.

363
00:30:36,750 --> 00:30:38,230
- Wait.
- Oh?

364
00:30:38,705 --> 00:30:40,415
It's too dangerous
for you to go alone.

365
00:30:41,466 --> 00:30:43,365
I don't get why.

366
00:30:43,727 --> 00:30:45,938
I mean, even if the
Roswells see me,

367
00:30:46,452 --> 00:30:48,287
they don't know
I'm part of Swansea.

368
00:30:48,856 --> 00:30:49,891
So, I'll be good.

369
00:30:49,916 --> 00:30:51,876
Just relax, okay?

370
00:30:52,310 --> 00:30:53,920
Okay. Hurry, okay?

371
00:31:04,399 --> 00:31:05,399
Jerson.

372
00:31:06,291 --> 00:31:07,300
Aux.

373
00:31:07,325 --> 00:31:09,661
Why don't we just kill Arcadia?

374
00:31:11,704 --> 00:31:13,540
Since we're already here anyway.

375
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:18,169
Let's just follow
Violet's plan for now.

376
00:31:19,078 --> 00:31:20,078
Okay?

377
00:31:40,608 --> 00:31:41,985
What are you looking at?

378
00:31:43,736 --> 00:31:44,736
Let's go.

379
00:31:48,283 --> 00:31:49,283
Ha...

380
00:31:51,703 --> 00:31:52,703
Nothing.

381
00:31:59,961 --> 00:32:00,961
I'm gonna have a smoke.

382
00:32:07,427 --> 00:32:08,427
Ah, shit.

383
00:32:09,095 --> 00:32:10,095
Miss Aemie.

384
00:32:12,348 --> 00:32:14,017
Who are you visiting here?

385
00:32:14,934 --> 00:32:16,060
Uhh.

386
00:32:16,728 --> 00:32:18,354
I-I... You! You.

387
00:32:18,354 --> 00:32:19,355
I was hoping it was you.

388
00:32:22,942 --> 00:32:23,943
Ahh.

389
00:32:30,450 --> 00:32:31,451
Uhh.

390
00:32:36,205 --> 00:32:37,457
Are you following me?

391
00:32:39,208 --> 00:32:40,543
It's just that, Miss Aemie...

392
00:32:40,543 --> 00:32:41,543
Uh...

393
00:32:41,836 --> 00:32:43,880
No, I'm not. It's just...

394
00:32:46,799 --> 00:32:48,426
You're Ezekiel's friend, right?

395
00:32:49,513 --> 00:32:50,762
Yes.

396
00:32:50,880 --> 00:32:51,880
We used to be.

397
00:32:52,347 --> 00:32:54,390
But we don't talk anymore.

398
00:32:56,869 --> 00:32:58,120
You should be thankful.

399
00:33:01,631 --> 00:33:03,006
Wait, hold on.

400
00:33:03,260 --> 00:33:04,300
Just a moment, Miss Aemie.

401
00:33:04,525 --> 00:33:07,236
Maybe you'd like to
have dinner with me first.

402
00:33:09,906 --> 00:33:11,066
I still have something to do.

403
00:33:11,699 --> 00:33:12,699
Oh.

404
00:33:13,576 --> 00:33:14,576
Okay.

405
00:33:34,639 --> 00:33:35,639
Aemie.

406
00:33:42,397 --> 00:33:43,773
How do you feel?

407
00:33:46,401 --> 00:33:47,985
I'm okay.

408
00:33:49,195 --> 00:33:50,195
How about you?

409
00:33:51,614 --> 00:33:52,949
Are you okay, Aemie?

410
00:33:53,741 --> 00:33:55,159
You don't remember anything?

411
00:34:04,419 --> 00:34:05,420
Yes.

412
00:34:06,796 --> 00:34:08,548
But not totally.

413
00:34:09,382 --> 00:34:11,008
When I got shot that—

414
00:34:12,260 --> 00:34:14,679
Lee said is
what I don't remember.

415
00:34:28,985 --> 00:34:30,445
Is there a problem, Fauzia?

416
00:34:34,282 --> 00:34:35,282
Nothing.

417
00:34:36,117 --> 00:34:37,243
Because—

418
00:34:38,453 --> 00:34:40,538
because Ezekiel
might be looking for you.

419
00:34:42,957 --> 00:34:43,957
Don't worry.

420
00:34:46,169 --> 00:34:47,378
We're over.

421
00:34:48,880 --> 00:34:50,131
I'm still waiting for someone.

422
00:35:00,641 --> 00:35:02,059
What are you doing?

423
00:35:10,026 --> 00:35:11,026
Aemie?

424
00:35:30,630 --> 00:35:31,630
Eat.

425
00:35:31,964 --> 00:35:32,964
You're looking pale.

426
00:35:52,985 --> 00:35:54,111
Ma'am, excuse me.

427
00:35:54,320 --> 00:35:56,322
The patient needs
to take her medicine—

428
00:35:56,322 --> 00:35:58,074
I'll give her the medicine.

429
00:35:58,783 --> 00:36:00,159
Oh, ma'am. I'm sorry.

430
00:36:00,159 --> 00:36:03,376
- You can't—
- I am a BS Biology student.

431
00:36:04,080 --> 00:36:05,669
I know about different drugs,

432
00:36:05,694 --> 00:36:07,529
and how to administer
them properly.

433
00:36:07,553 --> 00:36:08,637
So definitely...

434
00:36:09,963 --> 00:36:12,711
I can manage giving
Miss Arcadia her dose.

435
00:36:14,168 --> 00:36:16,008
I'll just have to give
her the medicine, right?

436
00:36:16,711 --> 00:36:17,921
That's not so hard.

437
00:36:19,585 --> 00:36:20,585
Give it to me.

438
00:36:25,393 --> 00:36:26,393
Here, ma'am.

439
00:36:27,186 --> 00:36:29,005
There's two medicines
she has to take.

440
00:36:29,030 --> 00:36:30,030
I know.

441
00:36:32,382 --> 00:36:33,390
Get out now.

442
00:36:33,415 --> 00:36:34,416
I can handle it.

443
00:36:48,917 --> 00:36:49,918
Do you have a...

444
00:36:50,418 --> 00:36:51,919
history of hypertension?

445
00:36:52,469 --> 00:36:53,762
Hypertension?

446
00:36:54,630 --> 00:36:55,923
I don't think so.

447
00:36:57,120 --> 00:36:58,120
Why?

448
00:37:02,763 --> 00:37:04,182
Take this pain reliever...

449
00:37:04,807 --> 00:37:06,767
so that you can
manage your injuries.

450
00:37:07,082 --> 00:37:08,082
Aemie.

451
00:37:08,202 --> 00:37:09,202
Hold on.

452
00:37:10,938 --> 00:37:14,184
Didn't the nurse gave
you two medicines?

453
00:37:15,235 --> 00:37:16,235
Don't worry.

454
00:37:16,882 --> 00:37:18,216
She made a mistake.

455
00:37:18,867 --> 00:37:19,867
You don't need it.

456
00:37:23,284 --> 00:37:24,284
Just take a rest.

457
00:38:03,908 --> 00:38:04,908
Love.

458
00:38:06,202 --> 00:38:07,703
Do you know what
this meeting is for?

459
00:38:10,164 --> 00:38:11,582
I have no idea.

460
00:38:12,583 --> 00:38:14,627
I am the one who
called this meeting.

461
00:38:16,087 --> 00:38:17,087
Shall we start?

462
00:38:20,132 --> 00:38:21,175
First of all,

463
00:38:22,134 --> 00:38:24,679
I invited everyone
for a celebration.

464
00:38:28,933 --> 00:38:30,559
My dad has told me,

465
00:38:31,310 --> 00:38:35,106
how much the Swanseas
have helped our family.

466
00:38:37,900 --> 00:38:38,943
So, Auntie Violet...

467
00:38:40,277 --> 00:38:42,321
from the bottom of my heart,

468
00:38:42,947 --> 00:38:43,947
thank you.

469
00:38:44,532 --> 00:38:47,827
You're always very welcome dear.

470
00:38:48,619 --> 00:38:50,621
Anything for your daddy.

471
00:38:52,665 --> 00:38:55,418
And to extend my
gratitude to the Swanseas,

472
00:38:57,128 --> 00:38:58,254
From now on,

473
00:38:59,755 --> 00:39:03,050
we will form an alliance.

474
00:39:04,593 --> 00:39:08,264
Yaji and Swanseas
will work as one.

475
00:39:28,325 --> 00:39:30,161
As the Yaji heiress,

476
00:39:30,870 --> 00:39:34,498
I have the power to decide
our next steps moving forward.

477
00:39:35,458 --> 00:39:38,836
Once my annulment with
Ezekiel Roswell is approved,

478
00:39:40,337 --> 00:39:43,716
we'll start bringing
down the Roswells.

479
00:39:44,290 --> 00:39:47,919
We will show no mercy.

480
00:39:49,805 --> 00:39:51,724
We will take down
their businesses

481
00:39:52,763 --> 00:39:56,141
and we'll take them down one by one.

482
00:39:57,678 --> 00:39:58,678
This.

483
00:39:59,083 --> 00:40:00,083
Is.

484
00:40:00,108 --> 00:40:01,118
War.

485
00:40:01,186 --> 00:40:05,607
We should wait for the queen to
wake up before we make any rash move.

486
00:40:05,963 --> 00:40:08,758
We don't know what
the consequences could be—

487
00:40:08,783 --> 00:40:10,503
Are you going against me,
Cassandra Heather?

488
00:40:11,520 --> 00:40:12,687
No.

489
00:40:13,871 --> 00:40:15,331
How disrespectful.

490
00:40:15,626 --> 00:40:16,794
Excuse me?

491
00:40:17,750 --> 00:40:18,918
What did you say?

492
00:40:19,455 --> 00:40:20,831
You heard what I said.

493
00:40:21,378 --> 00:40:23,547
You know what?
That's not disrespectful.

494
00:40:23,756 --> 00:40:25,591
She was just making a—

495
00:40:25,671 --> 00:40:27,923
Ladies, calm down.

496
00:40:28,596 --> 00:40:29,764
Let's hear Aemie first.

497
00:40:31,037 --> 00:40:32,239
Yeah, I'm listening but—

498
00:40:32,264 --> 00:40:33,264
Enough!

499
00:40:36,166 --> 00:40:39,794
We are launching a
war against the Roswells.

500
00:40:45,986 --> 00:40:50,950
We'll bring down
Ezekiel Roswell once and for all!

501
00:40:57,607 --> 00:40:59,651
It's so beautiful!

502
00:40:59,651 --> 00:41:01,863
It's so pink! So beautiful!

503
00:41:01,888 --> 00:41:03,488
It's so pink!

504
00:41:06,658 --> 00:41:08,451
Just in case...

505
00:41:08,660 --> 00:41:10,971
she won't wake up anymore.

506
00:41:10,996 --> 00:41:12,205
Get out of my room.

507
00:41:12,330 --> 00:41:14,582
We keep ending up together.

508
00:41:15,019 --> 00:41:17,209
Oh, you.

509
00:41:21,280 --> 00:41:22,280
Annulment?

510
00:41:22,573 --> 00:41:23,949
Don't worry, dear.

511
00:41:23,974 --> 00:41:26,143
I'll make the annulment
process quick.

512
00:41:33,334 --> 00:41:34,391
[screams]

513
00:41:34,519 --> 00:41:35,519
Mommy!

514
00:41:35,548 --> 00:41:37,296
Don't shout, Baby Ae!

515
00:41:37,605 --> 00:41:38,732
Oh!

516
00:41:41,776 --> 00:41:43,945
Hey! Open this door!

517
00:41:44,487 --> 00:41:45,739
Open this!

518
00:41:47,073 --> 00:41:48,617
Who's this bitch?
